#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""orionx-cockpit — the Orion-X live cockpit: SEE the cyber activity around you.

A full-window Cairo dashboard that consumes the same event bus R.A.I.N. sounds
(/run/orionx/events.jsonl) plus non-privileged host telemetry, and renders it
as animated instruments:

    ┌──────────────────────── ORION-X // COCKPIT ── posture ── clock ──┐
    │  EVENT STREAM (live, severity-coloured,  │  THREAT PRESSURE gauge  │
    │  newest first, fades with age; warning/  │  (decaying severity)    │
    │  critical events FLASH the whole deck —  ├─────────────────────────┤
    │  the visual twin of the R.A.I.N. tone)   │  NETWORK  rx/tx spark   │
    │                                          ├─────────────────────────┤
    │                                          │  SYSTEMS  LEDs          │
    └──────────────────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────┘

Keys (LIVE): Up/Down select · Enter detail · s/t squelch/tune in detail ·
PgUp/PgDn scroll (in detail: page) · a approve · Esc close detail / leave
fullscreen · F11 fullscreen · Alt+1..8 tabs · Ctrl+Q quit (UX-47: a stray q
or Esc no longer closes the live view). Ctrl+PgUp/PgDn switch tabs (GTK).
Flags: --fullscreen, --demo (synthetic events, for demos/screenshots).

GLib timers drive polling (events 0.5s, network 1s, systems 5s, vitals 2s) and
a ~6 fps redraw. Anything that forks (systemctl, pgrep, ip, orionx-heal,
orionx-tune) runs in a worker thread and only while LIVE is the visible tab;
results are applied on the main loop (DEC-PHASE12-068). All logic that is not
drawing lives in cockpit_lib.py (dependency-free, unit-tested). DEC-PHASE12-007.
"""

